# Index / landing-pose gate on the pentagon numeral shell in landing.scad
# (selftest: PASS). At each of the five stops the presenting face must land
# flat within tolerance and its numeral must read upright and right-handed;
# the rolled and mirrored poses prove every check can fail.
stops stop 0,1,2,3,4
empty landing-flat                          # posed shell ∩ beyond-the-face slab
empty landing-flat-in-tol                   # the same, rolled by half the tolerance
nonempty landing-glyph                      # posed numeral ∩ the chiral-stroke probe
empty landing-glyph-cover                   # shrunk upright template − posed numeral
empty-control landing-flat-rolled           # mis-landed by 20°: must poke through
empty-control landing-glyph-cover-mirrored  # mirrored numeral: template stroke uncovered
nonempty-control landing-glyph-mirrored     # mirrored numeral: stroke on the other side
nonempty-control landing-glyph-rolled       # rolled numeral: stroke off the probe
